    "body": "## Problem\n\n`PrimeRewardManager` crashes the result-processing loop of `parallel_compute_score_async` with `KeyError: 0` whenever the reward function returns a dict such as `{\"score\": 1.0, \"acc\": true, \"pred\": \"42\"}` — exactly what `math_dapo.compute_score`, `rlla.compute_score` and several custom reward functions return. The exception is swallowed by `PrimeRewardManager.verify`, so the entire batch is silently scored 0.0 and the RL reward signal is destroyed.\n\n## Fix\n\nHandle dict-shaped results in the result-processing loop by extracting `result[\"score\"]`, matching the existing behavior of `NaiveRewardManager`, `BatchRewardManager` and `DAPORewardManager`.\n\n## Test\n\nAdded `tests/workers/reward_manager/test_prime_on_cpu.py` covering both dict and float score paths.\n\nFixes #8216",
    "changed_files": 2,
    "closed_at": null,
